eserved & Enhanced AI Services**:\n   * **Multi-Stop Route Planner (`/api/ai/route`)**: Retained OpenAI GPT-4o-mini and Google Routes API integrations. Added **Google Gemini API** (`google-genai` SDK) and a built-in rule-based NLP parser with Haversine distance calculations.\n   * **AI Natural Language Trip Logger (`/api/ai/parse-trip`)**: Automatically parses unstructured travel descriptions (voice/text) into structured NATPAC survey fields (`origin`, `destination`, `travel_mode`, `departure_time`, `trip_purpose`, `fare_cost`).\n   * **Smart Tourism Itinerary Generator (`/api/ai/itinerary`)**: Generates custom 2-to-7 day itineraries with daily schedules, local culinary recommendations, and sustainable transit modes.\n\n3. **Real-World Online Tourism APIs**:\n   * **OpenStreetMap / Nominatim API**: Geocoding and reverse geocoding to auto-fill location names, roads, districts, and coordinates.\n   * **Wikivoyage / Wikipedia MediaWiki REST API**: Live destination summaries, cultural heritage details, and sightseeing information.\n   * **Open-Meteo Live Weather API**: Real-time temperature (°C), weather conditions, humidity, and forecasts without requiring API keys.\n   * **Organized Tourism Attributes**: Food & Local Cuisine 🍛, S\n<truncated 2768 bytes>\nstandalone ES6 frontend client.\n* [frontend/manifest.webmanifest](file:///C:/Users/akhil/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/frontend/manifest.webmanifest) & [frontend/sw.js](file:///C:/Users/akhil/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/frontend/sw.js): PWA installable manifest and offline service worker.\n* [tests/test_app.py](file:///C:/Users/akhil/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/tests/test_app.py): Automated test suite covering all API endpoints.\n* [run.py](file:///C:/Users/akhil/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/run.py): One-click server runner.\n* [requirements.txt](file:///C:/Users/akhil/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/requirements.txt): Python dependencies.\n* [walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/akhil/.gemini/antigravity/brain/b9e18599-ebc1-4ec3-9c72-c50606067964/walkthrough.md): Walkthrough documentation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Tests & Verification Performed\n\n* **Automated Unit Tests**: All 9 test cases in `tests/test_app.py` passed (`Ran 9 tests in 0.213s — OK`).\n* **Live Server Verification**: Started server on `http://127.0.0.1:8787` and verified:\n  * Database connection and status (`/api/status` -> 200 OK)\n  * NATPAC trip creation and listing (`/api/trips` -> 200/201 OK)\n  * AI multi-stop route calculation (`/api/ai/route` -> 200 OK)\n  * AI natural language trip extraction (`/api/ai/parse-trip` -> 200 OK)\n  * Real-world live tourism data retrieval (`/api/tourism/fetch-live` -> 200 OK for *Varkala*)\n  * GPS reverse geocoding (`/api/geocode/reverse` -> 200 OK for *Thiruvananthapuram*)\n  * Transportation planning analytics (`/api/analytics/summary`, `/api/analytics/mode-split`, `/api/analytics/export/csv` -> 200 OK)\n  * Raw SQL query runner (`/api/query` -> 200 OK)\n  * Static file and PWA manifest serving (`/`, `/manifest.webmanifest`, `/src/styles.css`, `/src/main.js` -> 200 OK)\n\n---\n\n### 4. Setup and Run Commands\n\n```bash\n# 1. Install dependencies\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# 2. Run the application\npython run.py\n\n# 3. Run automated tests\npython -m unittest discover tests\n```\n\n*Access the application at **`http://localhost:8787`**.*","truncated_fields":["content"]}
