: \n20: - `android sdk install <package>[@<version>]...`: Install specific packages. Multiple packages can be specified, separated by spaces. `<version>` defaults to latest. For example: `android\n<truncated 12255 bytes>\nall  Install SDK packages\n238:             update   Update one or all packages to the latest version\n239:             remove   Remove packages from the SDK\n240:             list     List installed and available SDK packages\n241: \n242: skills\n243:           Usage: android skills [-h] [COMMAND]\n244:           Manage Android CLI skills. Includes commands to install, remove, list, and\n245:           search for skills by keyword.\n246:             -h, --help   Show this help message and exit.\n247:           Commands:\n248:             add     [id]      Install a specific skill by its ID to your environment\n249:             remove  [id]      Remove an installed skill by its ID\n250:             list              List installed and available skills\n251:             find    [keyword] Search for available skills in the repository matching a\n252:                       keyword\n253: \n254: studio\n255:           Usage: android studio [-h] [COMMAND]\n256:           Android Studio commands\n257:             -h, --help   Show this help message and exit.\n258:           Commands:\n259:             find-declaration        Find declaration of a symbol\n260:             find-usages             Find usages of a symbol\n261:             open-file               Open a file in Android Studio\n262:             check                   Check the status of running Studio instances\n263:             analyze-file            Analyze a file in Android Studio\n264:             render-compose-preview  Render a Compose preview in Android Studio\n265:             version-lookup          Looks up the latest available versions on the\n266:                                       internet of maven artifacts, Android versions, and\n267:                                       more.\n268: \n269: update\n270:           Usage: android update [--url=PARAM]\n271:           Update the Android CLI to the latest version.\n272:                 --url=PARAM   The URL to download the update from\n273: \n274: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
